+### 5c — Mini-charter backstop (cost tracking, CONTRACTS §10.3)
+
+**When `issue_ref` is present**, check the issue body for a `<!-- falcon:charter:v1` marker
+(you already read the body in earlier steps for grounding; a cached read is fine). If it is
+ABSENT, create the mini-charter NOW — marker on the issue body + 🧭 Team-plan card in the
+thread — exactly per `process-github-event.md` Step 1.7. This is the deterministic
+open-if-missing backstop (mirrors the release-thread pattern): Step 1.7 only fires on
+`issues.opened` kickoffs, so issues that enter the pipeline mid-life — label events, stall
+recovery, priority:asap, anything predating a session restart — would otherwise never get a
+charter, and their ledger rows would carry `planned: null` (the 2026-08-07 snapdex#995 gap).
+For the `planned` crew on a mid-pipeline backstop, list the remaining expected stages from the
+CURRENT stage_label forward — don't reconstruct history; the usage reports are the record of
+what already happened. Non-blocking on failure (log + proceed to Step 6); never edit an
+existing charter marker.
